	<entry>
		<title>Madonna To Team Up With Lourdes For New Music?</title>
		<link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="http://drownedmadonna.com/index/item/7-madonna-to-team-up-with-lourdes-for-new-music?.html"/>
		<published>2011-05-11T15:38:22Z</published>
		<updated>2011-05-11T15:38:22Z</updated>
		<id>http://drownedmadonna.com/index/item/7-madonna-to-team-up-with-lourdes-for-new-music?.html</id>
		<author>
			<name>Vincenzo Ruocco</name>
		</author>
		<summary type="html">&lt;div class=&quot;K2FeedIntroText&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The 52-year-old recruited Lourdes for It's So Cool, a track which could also feature on Madge's next album, or on the soundtrack to her upcoming film, W.E., which she is directing. Find out more, click on Read More.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;K2FeedFullText&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A source told The Sun that Lourdes's foray into music is no gimmick, as she has a great voice and plenty of character.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The insider added: 'Madonna hopes Lourdes will step into her shoes and become one of the biggest female artists in the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;'She is the perfect mentor for her daughter and is keen to assist her first steps into the music industry.'&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The song in question was actually recorded acoustically by the pair back in 2003, but a subsequent release had Lourdes's vocals removed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;However, the single is not the only current collaboration between mother and daughter, with Madonna and Lourdes also working together on the Material Girl fashion line.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Kelly Osbourne was named as the new face of the clothing label back in January, replacing Gossip Girl star Taylor Momsen.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lourdes was supposedly the driving force behind the switch, with reports suggesting that the youngster 'idolises' Kelly.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;K2FeedTags&quot;&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Music&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Lola&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;W.E.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</summary>
